  "title": "Unified Title",
  "summary": "RoMo Hands provides a large-scale, richly organized text-to-hand motion dataset with 542K sequences, enabling robust generalization. ContextHands completes hand motion by integrating learned context and joint-specific body kinematics, improving realism and expressiveness.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "RoMo Hands contains ~542K sequences (884 hours, 95.5M frames) with a dexterity filter reducing low-articulation sequences.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "ContextHands learns probabilistic hand features from text and body motion, and uses a joint-specific body encoder for accurate hand motion completion.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "Both encoders and the generator are trained jointly to achieve improved hand motion and lower Fréchet Hand Distance compared to existing methods.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
